":"in need"},{"key":"B","text":"needing"},{"key":"C","text":"needed"},{"key":"D","text":"which need"}],"answer":"B"},{"n":3,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"inefficient"},{"key":"B","text":"efficient"},{"key":"C","text":"ineffective"},{"key":"D","text":"effective"}],"answer":"B"},{"n":4,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"Most"},{"key":"B","text":"Most of"},{"key":"C","text":"The most"},{"key":"D","text":"The most of"}],"answer":"A"},{"n":5,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"what"},{"key":"C","text":"but"},{"key":"D","text":"who"}],"answer":"A"},{"n":6,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"despite"},{"key":"B","text":"but"},{"key":"C","text":"although"},{"key":"D","text":"though"}],"answer":"D"},{"n":7,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"make"},{"key":"B","text":"take"},{"key":"C","text":"give"},{"key":"D","text":"do"}],"answer":"C"},{"n":8,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"worthy"},{"key":"B","text":"worthless"},{"key":"C","text":"worse"},{"key":"D","text":"worth"}],"answer":"D"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2006-febr-emelt-L2$mtr$, $mtr$2006-febr-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 2, $mtr$text$mtr$, $mtr$szóképzés (zárójeles szó)$mtr$, 9, 6, $mtr${"id":"2006-febr-emelt-L2","number":2,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about “green” buildings. Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (9-17).","Then write these words on the dotted lines after the text in the appropriate form.","You might find words that you do not have to change."],"title":"\"GREEN\" BUILDINGS MAY HELP SAVE ENVIRONMENT","body":["These days a green building means more than just the color of the paint. “Green” building can also refer to {{0}} friendly houses, factories, and offices. Green building means reducing the impact of the building on the land. Green buildings can reduce energy and water use. Also, the buildings are often located near public {{9}} such as buses and subways, so that people can drive their cars less. That could be good for the environment, because cars use lots of {{10}} resources, such as gasoline, and cause {{11}}. Green buildings are often built on {{12}} developed land, so that the buildings don't destroy forests or other wild habitats. The first green {{13}} high-rise building in the U.S. is called the Solaire. Its project {{14}} says: \"We've reduced our energy {{15}} by one-third and our water by 50 percent.\" The Solaire cuts energy in part by using solar power. On the face of the building there are panels. They absorb the sun's energy and convert it to {{16}}. The Solaire also has lights that {{17}} turn off when people leave the room. Plus, the building has lots of windows. This allows people to use the sun for light instead of lamps during the day."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict"},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"environment","example":true,"accept":["environmentally"]},{"n":9,"prompt":"transport"},{"n":10,"prompt":"nature"},{"n":11,"prompt":"pollute"},{"n":12,"prompt":"previous"},{"n":13,"prompt":"resident"},{"n":14,"prompt":"manage"},{"n":15,"prompt":"consume"},{"n":16,"prompt":"electric"},{"n":17,"prompt":"automatic"}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2006-febr-emelt-L2$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2006-febr-emelt-L2","number":2,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about “green” buildings. Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (9-17).","Then write these words on the dotted lines after the text in the appropriate form.","You might find words that you do not have to change."],"title":"\"GREEN\" BUILDINGS MAY HELP SAVE ENVIRONMENT","body":["These days a green building means more than just the color of the paint. “Green” building can also refer to {{0}} friendly houses, factories, and offices. Green building means reducing the impact of the building on the land. Green buildings can reduce energy and water use. Also, the buildings are often located near public {{9}} such as buses and subways, so that people can drive their cars less. That could be good for the environment, because cars use lots of {{10}} resources, such as gasoline, and cause {{11}}. Green buildings are often built on {{12}} developed land, so that the buildings don't destroy forests or other wild habitats. The first green {{13}} high-rise building in the U.S. is called the Solaire. Its project {{14}} says: \"We've reduced our energy {{15}} by one-third and our water by 50 percent.\" The Solaire cuts energy in part by using solar power. On the face of the building there are panels. They absorb the sun's energy and convert it to {{16}}. The Solaire also has lights that {{17}} turn off when people leave the room. Plus, the building has lots of windows. This allows people to use the sun for light instead of lamps during the day."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict","maxWords":1},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"environment","example":true,"accept":["environmentally"]},{"n":9,"prompt":"transport","accept":["transport","transportation"]},{"n":10,"prompt":"nature","accept":["natural"]},{"n":11,"prompt":"pollute","accept":["pollution"]},{"n":12,"prompt":"previous","accept":["previously"]},{"n":13,"prompt":"resident","accept":["residential"]},{"n":14,"prompt":"manage","accept":["manager","management"]},{"n":15,"prompt":"consume","accept":["consumption"]},{"n":16,"prompt":"electric","accept":["electricity"]},{"n":17,"prompt":"automatic","accept":["automatically"]}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2006-febr-emelt-L3$mtr$, $mtr$2006-febr-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 3, $mtr$text$mtr$, $mtr$nyílt cloze (egy szó)$mtr$, 11, 7, $mtr${"id":"2006-febr-emelt-L3","number":3,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"nyílt cloze (egy szó)","points":11,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about the negative effects of flying long distances. Some words are missing from the text.","Your task is to write the missing words on the dotted lines (18-28) after the text.","Use only one word in each gap."],"title":"JET LAG","body":["The most important factor in jet lag is how {{0}} time zones you cross and travelling east seems to be worst for most people. Jet lag occurs when you cross over a number of time zones and disrupt the normal 24-hour rhythms, {{18}} help you wake up in the morning and go to sleep at night - also known {{19}} the 'body clock'.","{{20}} you have a rigid routine, it's likely that you might suffer more {{21}} someone who adapts easily to change. The symptoms of jet lag can include exhaustion, a feeling of disorientation and the inability to sleep. You may also feel dehydrated from {{22}} stuck in an air-conditioned cabin for hours and this can cause headaches, make {{23}} skin dry and make you more susceptible to colds or viruses.","Counteracting jet lag: • change your watch as soon as you {{24}} on the flight • a glass of wine during the flight has the effect of two to three glasses on the ground. Avoid feeling even worse with a hangover {{25}} reducing alcohol intake before and during your flight • walk up and down the aisle and {{26}} stretching exercises in your seat to reduce discomfort and to have a more relaxed flight • when you arrive {{27}} the new time zone, spend some time outside during daylight hours {{28}} natural light can help align your body clock • try to adjust your bedtime and mealtimes to the local timetable as soon as possible ."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict"},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"accept":["many"]},{"n":18},{"n":19},{"n":20},{"n":21},{"n":22},{"n":23},{"n":24},{"n":25},{"n":26},{"n":27},{"n":28}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
