 the other clever gadgets around, he had been such a heavy","answer":"been"},{"n":43,"text":"turnstile. Edison replied him, \"Well, you see, everyone who pushes","answer":"him"},{"n":44,"text":"the turnstile around these pumps eight gallons of water into the tank","answer":"these"}],"outro":"on my roof.\" (Paw Prints Anecdotes)"}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2011-maj-emelt-H1$mtr$, $mtr$2011-maj-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$listening$mtr$, 1, $mtr$choice$mtr$, $mtr$igaz / hamis / a szöveg nem mondja (A/B/C)$mtr$, 12, 9, $mtr${"id":"2011-maj-emelt-H1","number":1,"kind":"choice","layout":"stems","examType":"igaz / hamis / a szöveg nem mondja (A/B/C)","points":12,"instructions":["In this section you will hear a strange story from a New York City policeman.","Your task will be to decide whether the following statements are true, false or we do not know because the text does not say, and write the appropriate letter in the boxes on the right. Write A if the statement is true, write B if the statement is false, and write C if the text does not say.","First, you will have some time to look at the task, and then we will play the whole recording in one piece.","Then, after a short pause, you will hear the recording again, but this time we will play the text in shorter sections to give you enough time to write down your answers."],"audio":{"file":"e_angol_11maj_fl.mp3","start":0,"end":672.27,"clip":"hang/e_angol_11maj_fl_H1.mp3"},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"Robert has believed in paranormal things all his life.","answer":"B"},{"n":1,"stem":"He went on a camping trip with his family."},{"n":2,"stem":"The local guide asked for a lot of money for his services."},{"n":3,"stem":"They saw the old man’s clothes but didn’t see his face."},{"n":4,"stem":"The old man walked past them without saying a word."},{"n":5,"stem":"The local guide said they had just seen the ghost of the mine road."},{"n":6,"stem":"Old Joe became a ghost because he had been murdered."},{"n":7,"stem":"Back in New York they never mentioned the ghost again."},{"n":8,"stem":"His partner knew that Robert would check the area alone."},{"n":9,"stem":"The guy who attacked him wanted his gun and money."},{"n":10,"stem":"The homeless guy stopped the attacker by shouting at him."},{"n":11,"stem":"Robert easily recognized Old Joe."},{"n":12,"stem":"Old Joe usually helps policemen."}],"options":[{"key":"A","text":"TRUE"},{"key":"B","text":"FALSE"},{"key":"C","text":"THE TEXT DOES NOT SAY"}]}$mtr$::jsonb, $mtr${"file":"e_angol_11maj_fl.mp3","start":0,"end":672.27,"clip":"hang/e_angol_11maj_fl_H1.mp3"}$mtr$::jsonb)
