ere is real diversity in the backgrounds of those who are doing this − there are builders, people in suits, people from all ethnicities.”","Police say in many cases those who were exploited had been told that they or their families back home would face violence if they reported what had happened to them. A man who was referred to Thames Reach by St Thomas’s hospital had been trafficked into the country by a gang. When he complained about not being paid, he was beaten up and left on the streets with brain damage. Other cases involved two Hungarian men who were held by criminals in Birmingham and forced to work on driveways, and a Czech man who was beaten by the owners of a car wash in north London before escaping.","The Department for Communities and Local Government has worked with the Passage Centre to fund a campaign to highlight the issue, and embassies in eastern Europe are also helping to raise awareness of the risk involved in working in the UK.","(The Observer)"],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"Thames Reach reveals that in the slave trade…","options":[{"key":"A","text":"an increasing number of cases get reported."},{"key":"B","text":"incidents are becoming more and more violent."},{"key":"C","text":"those forcing people to work for no pay break the law."},{"key":"D","text":"London has proved Britain’s worst afflicted area so far."}],"answer":"A"},{"n":25,"stem":"Megan Stewart says…","options":[{"key":"A","text":"charities have long urged the police to take tougher action in such cases."},{"key":"B","text":"people living near the Bedfordshire caravan site are getting worried."},{"key":"C","text":"people are too afraid to interfere when they spot signs of exploitation."},{"key":"D","text":"the police appear more willing to act in these cases than they used to be."}],"answer":"D"},{"n":26,"stem":"Mick Clarke, who runs a centre in Victoria, gives details of…","options":[{"key":"A","text":"various incidents when their clients were targeted by criminals."},{"key":"B","text":"one incident when their clients were targeted by criminals."},{"key":"C","text":"a case when their clients were tricked by Belgian criminals."},{"key":"D","text":"a case when their clients were given money and promised work in Belgium."}],"answer":"B"},{"n":27,"stem":"Clarke says traffickers…","options":[{"key":"A","text":"are more and more desperate."},{"key":"B","text":"are easy to recognise by their looks."},{"key":"C","text":"typically belong to one ethnic group."},{"key":"D","text":"are aided by the economic situation."}],"answer":"D"},{"n":28,"stem":"In a number of cases traffickers tried to silence their victims by…","options":[{"key":"A","text":"threats to them and their families."},{"key":"B","text":"giving them small rewards."},{"key":"C","text":"threatening to report them."},{"key":"D","text":"promises of extra pay."}],"answer":"A"},{"n":29,"stem":"Of the four victims mentioned in the last but one paragraph…","options":[{"key":"A","text":"one was sent to St Thomas’s from the Passage Centre."},{"key":"B","text":"two are described as having been subjected to physical violence."},{"key":"C","text":"two Hungarians were tourists travelling in the north of England."},{"key":"D","text":"the Czech man managed to escape with the help of the police."}],"answer":"B"},{"n":30,"stem":"To tackle the problem…","options":[{"key":"A","text":"local governments and homeless charities in Britain fund joint campaigns."},{"key":"B","text":"foreign embassies in London are asked to do more to help their citizens."},{"key":"C","text":"steps have been taken to make people more aware of the dangers."},{"key":"D","text":"job-seekers in eastern Europe are warned against working in Britain."}],"answer":"C"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2013-maj-emelt-L1$mtr$, $mtr$2013-maj-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 1, $mtr$text$mtr$, $mtr$szóképzés (zárójeles szó)$mtr$, 9, 5, $mtr${"id":"2013-maj-emelt-L1","number":1,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about an unfortunate error. Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (1-9).","There might be cases when you do not have to change the word in brackets.","Use only one word for each gap."],"title":"FRENCH WOMAN GETS 12 QUADRILLION PHONE BILL","body":["A French woman has been billed €11,721,000,000,000,000 for cancelling a phone contract. {{0}}, she will not have to pay the bill, which was sent out in error.","“I almost had a cardiac arrest! There were so many zeros I could not even work out how much it was”, said Solenne San Jose in an interview with French newspaper Sud Ouest.","The woman had asked to close her {{1}} account while she was out of work. Her service {{2}} said fine, but because it was going to be before the end of the contract she would have to pay a {{3}} fee. Ms San Jose was stunned to see a note at the bottom of the bill saying that the {{4}} sum would be taken from her bank account.","She called a helpline and tried to convince someone that a mistake had been made. This did not work {{5}}, and the person suggested that there was nothing that could be done, except perhaps paying the €12 quadrillion.","At some point common sense descended and someone at the firm understood that no {{6}} could possibly owe or pay a sum higher than France’s annual gross {{7}} output.","Following this {{8}} Ms San Jose was told that she must pay the much more {{9}} sum of €117.21. A spokesperson of Bouygues Telecom explained that the high number was there because of a machine error and added that as soon as the mistake was found the firm cancelled the bill, and sent the customer a bunch of flowers.","(http://www.theinquirer.net)"],"grading":{"spelling":"strict"},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"fortunate","example":true,"accept":["Fortunately"]},{"n":1,"prompt":"person"},{"n":2,"prompt":"provide"},{"n":3,"prompt":"cancel"},{"n":4,"prompt":"astonish"},{"n":5,"prompt":"initial"},{"n":6,"prompt":"individual"},{"n":7,"prompt":"economy"},{"n":8,"prompt":"realise"},{"n":9,"prompt":"reason"}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2013-maj-emelt-L1$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2013-maj-emelt-L1","number":1,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about an unfortunate error. Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (1-9).","There might be cases when you do not have to change the word in brackets.","Use only one word for each gap."],"title":"FRENCH WOMAN GETS 12 QUADRILLION PHONE BILL","body":["A French woman has been billed €11,721,000,000,000,000 for cancelling a phone contract. {{0}}, she will not have to pay the bill, which was sent out in error.","“I almost had a cardiac arrest! There were so many zeros I could not even work out how much it was”, said Solenne San Jose in an interview with French newspaper Sud Ouest.","The woman had asked to close her {{1}} account while she was out of work. Her service {{2}} said fine, but because it was going to be before the end of the contract she would have to pay a {{3}} fee. Ms San Jose was stunned to see a note at the bottom of the bill saying that the {{4}} sum would be taken from her bank account.","She called a helpline and tried to convince someone that a mistake had been made. This did not work {{5}}, and the person suggested that there was nothing that could be done, except perhaps paying the €12 quadrillion.","At some point common sense descended and someone at the firm understood that no {{6}} could possibly owe or pay a sum higher than France’s annual gross {{7}} output.","Following this {{8}} Ms San Jose was told that she must pay the much more {{9}} sum of €117.21. A spokesperson of Bouygues Telecom explained that the high number was there because of a machine error and added that as soon as the mistake was found the firm cancelled the bill, and sent the customer a bunch of flowers.","(http://www.theinquirer.net)"],"grading":{"spelling":"strict","maxWords":1},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"fortunate","example":true,"accept":["Fortunately"]},{"n":1,"prompt":"person","accept":["personal"]},{"n":2,"prompt":"provide","accept":["providers","provider"]},{"n":3,"prompt":"cancel","accept":["cancellation","cancelation"]},{"n":4,"prompt":"astonish","accept":["astonishing"]},{"n":5,"prompt":"initial","accept":["initially"]},{"n":6,"prompt":"individual","accept":["individual"]},{"n":7,"prompt":"economy","accept":["economic"]},{"n":8,"prompt":"realise","accept":["realization","realisation"]},{"n":9,"prompt":"reason","accept":["reasonable"]}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2013-maj-emelt-L2$mtr$, $mtr$2013-maj-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 2, $mtr$choice$mtr$, $mtr$feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)$mtr$, 10, 6, $mtr${"id":"2013-maj-emelt-L2","number":2,"kind":"choice","layout":"inline","examType":"feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)","points":10,"instructions":["You are going to read about an interesting discovery. Some words are missing from the text.","Choose the most appropriate answer from the options (A-D) for each gap (10-19) in the text."],"title":"BRITISH MUMMIES MADE UP OF THE BODIES OF DIFFERENT PEOPLE","body":["Archaeologists investigating the mystery of two perfectly {{0}} 3,000-year-old skeletons on a remote Scottish island believe they {{10}} made up of several different people.","The skeletons excavated in Cladh Hallan {{11}} the first evidence that Britons preserved their dead using mummification. But the identities of the oldest mummies {{12}} in Britain remain a great mystery {{13}} scientists have discovered they were made from body parts of several different people. Research last year {{14}} that the mummies were made up of parts from people in the same families and then put together {{15}} a jigsaw to make it look as if they were just one person.","Sheffield University Professor Mike Parker Pearson said the mummies {{16}} straight after preservation and are similar to those found in distant Peru in South America: “I {{17}} believe these mummies were buried immediately, but played an active part in society, as they do in some tribal societies in other parts of the world. As part of worship, the mummies probably would have been asked for spiritual advice to help the community {{18}} decisions.”","Archaeologists found the mummies in the foundations of a row of unusual Bronze Age terraced roundhouses. But {{19}} radiocarbon dated, all were found to have died between 300 and 500 years before the houses were built, meaning they had been kept above ground for some time by their descendants.","(www.dailymail.co.uk)"],"items":[{"n":0,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"reserved"},{"key":"B","text":"stayed"},{"key":"C","text":"preserved"},{"key":"D","text":"remained"}],"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":10,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"should be"},{"key":"B","text":"may have been"},{"key":"C","text":"would be"},{"key":"D","text":"ought to have been"}]},{"n":11,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"are told to be"},{"key":"B","text":"prove as"},{"key":"C","text":"are said to be"},{"key":"D","text":"reveal as"}]},{"n":12,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"nearly discovered"},{"key":"B","text":"ever found"},{"key":"C","text":"yet to be explored"},{"key":"D","text":"that examined"}]},{"n":13,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"as"},{"key":"B","text":"therefore"},{"key":"C","text":"so that"},{"key":"D","text":"because of"}]},{"n":14,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"introduced"},{"key":"B","text":"noticed"},{"key":"C","text":"regarded"},{"key":"D","text":"revealed"}]},{"n":15,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"like"},{"key":"B","text":"such as"},{"key":"C","text":"as though"},{"key":"D","text":"being"}]},{"n":16,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"did not bury"},{"key":"B","text":"have not been buried"},{"key":"C","text":"could not bury"},{"key":"D","text":"had not been buried"}]},{"n":17,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"firmly"},{"key":"B","text":"shouldn’t"},{"key":"C","text":"don’t"},{"key":"D","text":"will"}]},{"n":18,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"make"},{"key":"B","text":"makes"},{"key":"C","text":"made"},{"key":"D","text":"that make"}]},{"n":19,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"despite"},{"key":"B","text":"unless"},{"key":"C","text":"even"},{"key":"D","text":"when"}]}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2013-maj-emelt-L2$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2013-maj-emelt-L2","number":2,"kind":"choice","layout":"inline","examType":"feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)","points":10,"instructions":["You are going to read about an interesting discovery. Some words are missing from the text.","Choose the most appropriate answer from the options (A-D) for each gap (10-19) in the text."],"title":"BRITISH MUMMIES MADE UP OF THE BODIES OF DIFFERENT PEOPLE","body":["Archaeologists investigating the mystery of two perfectly {{0}} 3,000-year-old skeletons on a remote Scottish island believe they {{10}} made up of several different people.","The skeletons excavated in Cladh Hallan {{11}} the first evidence that Britons preserved their dead using mummification. But the identities of the oldest mummies {{12}} in Britain remain a great mystery {{13}} scientists have discovered they were made from body parts of several different people. Research last year {{14}} that the mummies were made up of parts from people in the same families and then put together {{15}} a jigsaw to make it look as if they were just one person.","Sheffield University Professor Mike Parker Pearson said the mummies {{16}} straight after preservation and are similar to those found in distant Peru in South America: “I {{17}} believe these mummies were buried immediately, but played an active part in society, as they do in some tribal societies in other parts of the world. As part of worship, the mummies probably would have been asked for spiritual advice to help the community {{18}} decisions.”","Archaeologists found the mummies in the foundations of a row of unusual Bronze Age terraced roundhouses. But {{19}} radiocarbon dated, all were found to have died between 300 and 500 years before the houses were built, meaning they had been kept above ground for some time by their descendants.","(www.dailymail.co.uk)"],"items":[{"n":0,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"reserved"},{"key":"B","text":"stayed"},{"key":"C","text":"preserved"},{"key":"D","text":"remained"}],"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":10,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"should be"},{"key":"B","text":"may have been"},{"key":"C","text":"would be"},{"key":"D","text":"ought to have been"}],"answer":"B"},{"n":11,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"are told to be"},{"key":"B","text":"prove as"},{"key":"C","text":"are said to be"},{"key":"D","text":"reveal as"}],"answer":"C"},{"n":12,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"nearly discovered"},{"key":"B","text":"ever found"},{"key":"C","text":"yet to be explored"},{"key":"D","text":"that examined"}],"answer":"B"},{"n":13,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"as"},{"key":"B","text":"therefore"},{"key":"C","text":"so that"},{"key":"D","text":"because of"}],"answer":"A"},{"n":14,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"introduced"},{"key":"B","text":"noticed"},{"key":"C","text":"regarded"},{"key":"D","text":"revealed"}],"answer":"D"},{"n":15,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"like"},{"key":"B","text":"such as"},{"key":"C","text":"as though"},{"key":"D","text":"being"}],"answer":"A"},{"n":16,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"did not bury"},{"key":"B","text":"have not been buried"},{"key":"C","text":"could not bury"},{"key":"D","text":"had not been buried"}],"answer":"D"},{"n":17,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"firmly"},{"key":"B","text":"shouldn’t"},{"key":"C","text":"don’t"},{"key":"D","text":"will"}],"answer":"C"},{"n":18,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"make"},{"key":"B","text":"makes"},{"key":"C","text":"made"},{"key":"D","text":"that make"}],"answer":"A"},{"n":19,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"despite"},{"key":"B","text":"unless"},{"key":"C","text":"even"},{"key":"D","text":"when"}],"answer":"D"}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2013-maj-emelt-L3$mtr$, $mtr$2013-maj-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 3, $mtr$text$mtr$, $mtr$nyílt cloze (egy szó)$mtr$, 9, 7, $mtr${"id":"2013-maj-emelt-L3","number":3,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"nyílt cloze (egy szó)","points":9,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about a popular cafe. Some words are missing from the text.","Your task is to write the missing words on the dotted lines (20-28) after the text.","Use only one word in each gap."],"title":"THE CAFE THAT PUT MICHELIN-STARRED RESTAURANTS IN THE SHADE","body":["With its comfy chairs, wooden fireplace and shabby chic lamp shades, it could very easily {{0}} mistaken for someone’s front room. But it is, in fact, a humble cafe {{20}} offers a full fried breakfast for the unremarkable price of £5.95 – including tea or coffee.","Now The Haven {{21}} been rated the best place to eat in Edinburgh. Every customer to review the cafe on the Trip Advisor website has given it the highest possible marks for food, service, value and atmosphere, {{22}} that it now ranks higher than the city’s five Michelin star restaurants. All five were awarded a star in the 2013 edition of the Michelin Red Guide but while they typically serve pigeon, deer and rabbit at around £70 a head for three courses, The Haven is a much {{23}} modest affair.","Its menu includes scones, cakes and pancakes all freshly {{24}} by cafe owner and University of Edinburgh graduate Natalie Kwek, 26. Natalie, {{25}} has a master’s degree in English, says the most popular dish is her fried Scottish breakfast – sausage, bacon, black pudding, haggis, fried eggs, baked beans, tomatoes, mushrooms, potato scones, toast and a cup of tea or coffee, for just £5.95.","Natalie, {{26}} cafe is in Newhaven, said: ‘I can’t believe it’s being mentioned in the same breath {{27}} these amazing Michelin star restaurants. To see my cafe rated above them on Trip Advisor is a real honour. When I opened the Haven last November, I hoped it {{28}} be something special but never imagined such success.’","(www.dailymail.co.uk)"],"grading":{"spelling":"strict"},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"accept":["be"]},{"n":20},{"n":21},{"n":22},{"n":23},{"n":24},{"n":25},{"n":26},{"n":27},{"n":28}]}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
