ell as their breathing, heartbeat, and muscle activity.","gapCount":2},{"n":18,"stem":"It’s been confirmed that all {{gap}} and {{gap}} studied with the EEG do actually sleep.","gapCount":2},{"n":19,"stem":"At the same time, however, there is some {{gap}} that {{gap}}, such as snakes and turtles do not truly sleep.","gapCount":2},{"n":20,"stem":"Good sleepers are nearly all {{gap}}, while poor sleepers are animals that are prey for predators, so they must be watching out for {{gap}}.","gapCount":2}],"grading":{"spelling":"lenient"}}$mtr$::jsonb, $mtr${"file":"e_angol_13maj_fl.mp3","start":604.57,"end":1211.05,"clip":"hang/e_angol_13maj_fl_H2.mp3"}$mtr$::jsonb)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2013-maj-emelt-H2$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2013-maj-emelt-H2","number":2,"kind":"text","layout":"stems","examType":"mondatkiegészítés hallás után (két szó)","points":9,"instructions":["In this section, you will hear an interview with a university professor about the sleeping habits of animals.","Your task will be to complete the sentences with two words in each sentence. Please use the exact words that you hear in the recording.","First, you will have some time to study the task, and then we will play the whole recording in one piece.","Then, you will hear the recording again, but this time we will play the text in shorter sections to give you enough time to write down your answers."],"audio":{"file":"e_angol_13maj_fl.mp3","start":604.57,"end":1211.05,"clip":"hang/e_angol_13maj_fl_H2.mp3"},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"The question comes from Mr Simmons, one of the programme’s {{gap}} {{gap}}","gaps":[["regular"],["listeners"]]},{"n":12,"stem":"In theory, if an animal stops its activities and stays {{gap}} and {{gap}}, we could assume that it is sleeping.","unordered":true,"gaps":[["quiet"],["unmoving"]]},{"n":13,"stem":"Factors such as the animal’s eyes and its physical activity, as well as whether it responds to {{gap}} or {{gap}}, might all indicate whether it is asleep or not.","unordered":true,"gaps":[["light"],["sound"]]},{"n":14,"stem":"Some animals rarely close their eyes while they sleep, whereas others, such as {{gap}} and {{gap}} cannot close them at all.","unordered":true,"gaps":[["fish"],["snakes"]]},{"n":15,"stem":"Elephants often sleep standing up, while they rest their {{gap}} in the {{gap}} of a tree.","gaps":[["tusks"],["fork"]]},{"n":16,"stem":"More precise answers to this question can be expected from {{gap}} carried out in sleep {{gap}}.","gaps":[["experiments"],["laboratories"]]},{"n":17,"stem":"The EEG measures the animals’ {{gap}} {{gap}}, as well as their breathing, heartbeat, and muscle activity.","gaps":[["brain"],["signals"]]},{"n":18,"stem":"It’s been confirmed that all {{gap}} and {{gap}} studied with the EEG do actually sleep.","unordered":true,"gaps":[["birds"],["mammals"]]},{"n":19,"stem":"At the same time, however, there is some {{gap}} that {{gap}}, such as snakes and turtles do not truly sleep.","gaps":[["evidence"],["reptiles"]]},{"n":20,"stem":"Good sleepers are nearly all {{gap}}, while poor sleepers are animals that are prey for predators, so they must be watching out for {{gap}}.","gaps":[["hunters"],["enemies"]]}],"grading":{"spelling":"lenient","caseSensitive":false,"note":"Csak akkor adható pont, ha MINDKETTŐ szó elfogadható!"}}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
