e weekend."},{"key":"B","text":"he was heartbroken that the family hadn’t had any food in the fridge."}],"answer":["A"]},{"n":15,"stem":"At school …","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Firmino suddenly became very talkative when he wanted to play with a ball."},{"key":"B","text":"Pedro sometimes refused to give Firmino a ball."}],"answer":["B"]},{"n":16,"stem":"As a well-paid star footballer, Firmino …","options":[{"key":"A","text":"settled the medical bills of a family."},{"key":"B","text":"regularly donates some money to a hospital"}],"answer":["A","B"]}]}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2024-okt-emelt-H3$mtr$, $mtr$2024-okt-emelt$mtr$, $mtr$listening$mtr$, 3, $mtr$choice$mtr$, $mtr$igaz / hamis / a szöveg nem mondja (A/B/C)$mtr$, 9, 11, $mtr${"id":"2024-okt-emelt-H3","number":3,"kind":"choice","layout":"stems","examType":"igaz / hamis / a szöveg nem mondja (A/B/C)","points":9,"instructions":["In this section you will hear a museum guide describing a famous painting called Ophelia by the English painter, John Everett Millais.","Your task will be to decide whether the following statements are true, false or we do not know because the text does not say, and write the appropriate letter in the boxes on the right. Write A if the statement is true, write B if the statement is false, and write C if the text does not say.","First, you will have some time to study the task, and then we will play the whole recording in one piece.","Then, you will hear the recording again, but this time we will play the text in shorter sections to give you enough time to write down your answers."],"audio":{"file":"e_angol_24okt_fl.mp3","start":1192.41,"end":1795.43,"clip":"hang/e_angol_24okt_fl_H3.mp3"},"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"stem":"The museum guide says that the Millais painting is the first stop on the tour.","answer":"B"},{"n":17,"stem":"The antique dress Millais bought was extremely expensive."},{"n":18,"stem":"The flowers Millais painted were all mentioned in Shakespeare’s play."},{"n":19,"stem":"The violets in the picture symbolize innocence."},{"n":20,"stem":"With this picture, Millais’ most important aim was the accurate depiction of nature."},{"n":21,"stem":"Millais started painting the background of the picture in the middle of the 19th century."},{"n":22,"stem":"Millais enjoyed every minute of painting peacefully outside in nature."},{"n":23,"stem":"Elizabeth Siddal became a painter because of Millais’ influence."},{"n":24,"stem":"Millais didn’t realize that the candles had gone out."},{"n":25,"stem":"Elizabeth’s father had to settle the doctor’s bills."}],"options":[{"key":"A","text":"TRUE"},{"key":"B","text":"FALSE"},{"key":"C","text":"THE TEXT DOES NOT SAY"}]}$mtr$::jsonb, $mtr${"file":"e_angol_24okt_fl.mp3","start":1192.41,"end":1795.43,"clip":"hang/e_angol_24okt_fl_H3.mp3"}$mtr$::jsonb)
