of Britain's most beloved writers, was the author of more than 20 children's books."},{"key":"D","text":"He spent around four hours every day writing stories in his garden shed."},{"key":"E","text":"His height, 6 foot 6 inches, earned him the nickname, “Lofty”."},{"key":"F","text":"Roald Dahl was named after the famous Norwegian polar explorer, Roald Amundson."},{"key":"G","text":"Many of his characters and stories were inspired by places and people around him."},{"key":"H","text":"Roald Dahl loved to play around with words and invent new ones or meanings."},{"key":"I","text":"Before he became an author, Roald Dahl was a pilot for the Royal Air Force, and he also became a spy for the British Secret Service."}],"items":[{"n":0,"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":26,"answer":"H"},{"n":27,"answer":"D"},{"n":28,"answer":"G"},{"n":29,"answer":"I"},{"n":30,"answer":"A"}],"source":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/newsround/articles/cx2509xn419o"}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2026-maj-kozep-L1$mtr$, $mtr$2026-maj-kozep$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 1, $mtr$text$mtr$, $mtr$szóképzés (zárójeles szó)$mtr$, 8, 5, $mtr${"id":"2026-maj-kozep-L1","number":1,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":8,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about a special service dog. Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (1-8).","There might be cases when you do not have to change the word in brackets.","Use only one word for each gap."],"title":"HERCULES ON PATROL","body":["At West Virginia International Yeager Airport, Hercules patrols the mile-long airfield {{0}}. The border collie has an important job: ensuring the safety of passengers and crew by keeping birds and wildlife away from planes. Chris Keyser, the airport’s wildlife specialist and the dog’s {{1}}, says preventing a bird from hitting a plane can save {{2}} of lives.","Since 2018, Yeager management has employed the services of border collies to keep the planes safe. Hercules, the chief patrol dog, also spends time inside the terminal, calming {{3}} passengers and receiving affection.","Before his {{4}} at Yeager, Hercules trained for 18 months at Flyaway Geese Center in Charlotte, North Carolina, learning to herd geese and {{5}}, preparing for his vital role in keeping the airport safe.","When Hercules stepped onto Charleston’s airfield for the first time, “I held my {{6}},” Flyaway Geese manager Rebecca Gibson said. “But boy, he knew {{7}} what to do. It was his place. He’s done a(n) {{8}} job and has just been a great dog for them. We’re very proud of him.”","Along the way, Hercules became a local celebrity. He has his own Instagram and TikTok accounts and regularly hosts groups of schoolchildren."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict"},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"day","example":true,"accept":["daily"]},{"n":1,"prompt":"own"},{"n":2,"prompt":"lot"},{"n":3,"prompt":"nerve"},{"n":4,"prompt":"arrive"},{"n":5,"prompt":"sheep"},{"n":6,"prompt":"breathe"},{"n":7,"prompt":"immediate"},{"n":8,"prompt":"marvel"}],"source":"https://www.independent.co.uk/travel/news-and-advice/west-virginia-yeager-airport-dogs-birds-b2759843.html"}$mtr$::jsonb, null)
insert into public.task_keys (task_id, task) values ($mtr$2026-maj-kozep-L1$mtr$, $mtr${"id":"2026-maj-kozep-L1","number":1,"kind":"text","layout":"inline","examType":"szóképzés (zárójeles szó)","points":8,"instructions":["You are going to read an article about a special service dog. Some words are missing from the text.","Use the words in brackets to form the words that fit in the gaps (1-8).","There might be cases when you do not have to change the word in brackets.","Use only one word for each gap."],"title":"HERCULES ON PATROL","body":["At West Virginia International Yeager Airport, Hercules patrols the mile-long airfield {{0}}. The border collie has an important job: ensuring the safety of passengers and crew by keeping birds and wildlife away from planes. Chris Keyser, the airport’s wildlife specialist and the dog’s {{1}}, says preventing a bird from hitting a plane can save {{2}} of lives.","Since 2018, Yeager management has employed the services of border collies to keep the planes safe. Hercules, the chief patrol dog, also spends time inside the terminal, calming {{3}} passengers and receiving affection.","Before his {{4}} at Yeager, Hercules trained for 18 months at Flyaway Geese Center in Charlotte, North Carolina, learning to herd geese and {{5}}, preparing for his vital role in keeping the airport safe.","When Hercules stepped onto Charleston’s airfield for the first time, “I held my {{6}},” Flyaway Geese manager Rebecca Gibson said. “But boy, he knew {{7}} what to do. It was his place. He’s done a(n) {{8}} job and has just been a great dog for them. We’re very proud of him.”","Along the way, Hercules became a local celebrity. He has his own Instagram and TikTok accounts and regularly hosts groups of schoolchildren."],"grading":{"spelling":"strict","maxWords":1},"items":[{"n":0,"prompt":"day","example":true,"accept":["daily"]},{"n":1,"prompt":"own","accept":["owner"]},{"n":2,"prompt":"lot","accept":["lots"]},{"n":3,"prompt":"nerve","accept":["nervous","unnerved","nervy"]},{"n":4,"prompt":"arrive","accept":["arrival"]},{"n":5,"prompt":"sheep","accept":["sheep"]},{"n":6,"prompt":"breathe","accept":["breath"]},{"n":7,"prompt":"immediate","accept":["immediately"]},{"n":8,"prompt":"marvel","accept":["marvelous","marvellous"]}],"source":"https://www.independent.co.uk/travel/news-and-advice/west-virginia-yeager-airport-dogs-birds-b2759843.html"}$mtr$::jsonb) on conflict (task_id) do update set task = excluded.task;
insert into public.tasks (id, exam_id, section, number, kind, exam_type, points, position, content, audio) values ($mtr$2026-maj-kozep-L2$mtr$, $mtr$2026-maj-kozep$mtr$, $mtr$language$mtr$, 2, $mtr$choice$mtr$, $mtr$feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)$mtr$, 8, 6, $mtr${"id":"2026-maj-kozep-L2","number":2,"kind":"choice","layout":"inline","examType":"feleletválasztós szövegkiegészítés (A-D)","points":8,"instructions":["You are going to read a joke about a frog and an economics student. Some words are missing from the text.","Choose the most appropriate answer from the options (A-D) for each gap (9-16) in the text."],"title":"A MODERN TALE","body":["An economics graduate student {{0}} a road one day when a frog called out to him and said, “If you kiss me, I’ll turn into a beautiful princess.” He stopped, picked {{9}} the frog, and put it in his pocket. The frog spoke up again and said, “If you kiss me and turn me back into a beautiful princess, I will stay with you for {{10}} one week.” The graduate student took the frog out of his pocket, smiled at it, and {{11}} it to his pocket.","Desperate, the frog then cried out, “If you kiss me and turn me back into a princess, I’ll stay with you {{12}} as you want.” Again, the grad student took the frog out, smiled at it, and put it back into his pocket. Finally, the frog asked, “What is the matter? I have {{13}} you I’m a beautiful princess, that I’ll be your girlfriend and do anything you want. Why {{14}} you kiss me?” The student said, “Look, I’m an economist. I have no idea {{15}} it would be like to have a girlfriend. But a talking frog has to be {{16}} its weight in gold.”"],"items":[{"n":0,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"did cross"},{"key":"B","text":"has crossed"},{"key":"C","text":"was crossing"},{"key":"D","text":"could cross"}],"example":true,"answer":"C"},{"n":9,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"on"},{"key":"B","text":"out"},{"key":"C","text":"up"},{"key":"D","text":"over"}]},{"n":10,"options":[{"key":"A","text":"as